"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"overrides the font specified for the overall metronome element. This allows separate specification of a music"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"font for the beat-unit and a text font for the numeric value, in cases where a single metronome font is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"used."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlperminute","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPerMinute"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLPerMinute","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPerMinute"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPerMinute","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The metronome type represents metronome marks and other metric relationships. The beat-unit group and per-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"minute element specify regular metronome marks. The metronome-note and metronome-relation elements allow for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the specification of metric modulations and other metric relationships, such as swing tempo marks where two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"eighths are equated to a quarter note \/ eighth note triplet. Tied notes can be represented in both types of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"metronome marks by using the beat-unit-tied and metronome-tied elements. The parentheses attribute indicates"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whether or not to put the metronome mark in parentheses; its value is no if not specified. The print-object"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attribute is set to no in cases where the metronome element represents a relationship or range that is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"displayed in the music notation."}],"url":